-- Passage rg4-main-idea-summary-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('0fe97d06-e92f-5ad5-84d9-9eea6afce892', 'rg4-main-idea-summary-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-main-idea-summary'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Wheelchair Basketball$q$, $q$Wheelchair basketball is a fast and exciting sport. Players who use wheelchairs, as well as some who have leg injuries, can all play. The game is a lot like regular basketball, but a few rules are changed to fit the chairs.

The court and the hoop are the same size as in other basketball games. The ball is the same, too. Players still pass, dribble, and shoot at a basket ten feet high. Shooting from a seated position takes strong arms and lots of practice.

Some rules are different. A player may push the wheels twice while holding the ball. After that, the player must pass, shoot, or bounce the ball. Players can bump chairs a little, but they may not crash into each other on purpose.

The chairs are special, too. Sports wheelchairs are light and low to the ground. Their wheels tilt outward at the bottom. This shape helps players turn quickly without tipping over.

Today, wheelchair basketball is played in schools, clubs, and big international games. Teams practice hard and play with great skill. The sport shows that with a few smart changes, a game can welcome many more players.$q$, 'draft')
